      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>&hellip; take it from him just as your relative Yibqi b. &rsquo;Abu Razin took [him]</li>\n<li>&hellip; rather 250 gold pieces, which he sent, and he took them</li>\n<li>&hellip; news of them, their abuse and hard work. What is more, there is among them a young girl</li>\n<li>&hellip;m for her, so that they not abuse her. We constantly weep about the magnitude of our sins</li>\n<li>&hellip;and we were captured [and taken] from place to place. After all of this we took</li>\n<li>&hellip; [e]lderly and went to his tents, where we stayed in the heat of the day and the frost of the night</li>\n<li>&hellip; on our behalf to him, and we made a request of him. There then passed between us and him [i.e., the pirate, the relative of Yibqi b. Abu Razin] many words</li>\n<li>&hellip;to you from me an Edomite slave4 who is worth 20 gold pieces, so he brought him</li>\n<li>&ldquo;&hellip; take your brother and go.&rdquo; We told him that we could do no such thing</li>\n<li>&hellip;[for] we would be incurring a cost prohibited by religious obligation, as our sages taught us:</li>\n<li>&hellip; &ldquo;[one does not redeem] captives for more than their worth, to avoid encouraging the practice.&rdquo; So, we returned to</li>\n<li>&nbsp;&hellip;we&hellip; to our elder, Mar Rav Nathan ha-Kohen, may he live on, and to the rest of the holy congregation</li>\n<li>&hellip; these things. Rav Nathan responded and said, &ldquo;Let the matter rest until the money arrives &hellip;</li>\n<li>&hellip; I will deal in this matter as you wish and according to my ability &ndash; may God bring [me] success.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>&hellip; a letter from Mukhtar the Arab, and he said to him that he sent my son Jabarah</li>\n<li>&hellip; the Jews to the region of Barqah, but I will not send them, for your sake</li>\n<li>&hellip; after the entire community, and he recounted the entire story to them, but they said &ldquo;We cannot</li>\n<li>&hellip; from among the captives for 100 gold pieces, so he sent himresponses</li>\n<li>&hellip; &ldquo;you asked about them, and God will bring success to the endeavor and double his reward.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>&hellip; and they said &hellip; their privation, and since the slaves</li>\n<li>&hellip; our weeping on their behalf</li>\n<li>&hellip; to her</li></ol>\n",
